FPU - (C) 1995 Microware Systems Corp.Permission to distribute FPU is granted so long as this file is retained.Ultra C only generates one model of floating point code.  If no floatingpoint coprocessor is present in the system, the FPU floating point emulationsoftware module will make it appear like one exists.To use the floating point math functions on a 68K machine that doesnot have a math coprocessor, you must do the following:       1. Add the fpu module to your bootfile       2. Add fpu to the extension module list in your          Init module and remake it       3. Generate a new bootfile and reboot the system.